  user_input {
    user_response: "# Autonomous Full-Project Generation Prompt\n\n## Real ESP32 POV Hologram System (Production Grade)\n\nYou are an autonomous senior embedded systems engineer, full-stack IoT architect, PCB designer, and firmware developer.\n\nYour task is to FULLY DESIGN AND GENERATE a production-grade rotating POV hologram platform using ESP32 hardware.\n\nYou must behave like a real engineering team and autonomously make correct engineering decisions where specifications are missing.\n\nDO NOT ask unnecessary questions.\nDO NOT generate placeholder code.\nDO NOT generate pseudo-code unless absolutely necessary.\nDO NOT simplify the project into a demo.\nDO NOT generate fake hologram effects.\n\nEverything must be realistic, compilable, hardware-aware, and production-oriented.\n\n---\n\n# PROJECT GOAL\n\nBuild a REAL rotating POV hologram display with:\n\n* 2 rotating arms\n* 3 LED strips per arm\n* 45 LEDs per strip\n* Total: 270 LEDs\n* Hall sensor synchronization\n* Wi-Fi connectivity\n* Web dashboard\n* OTA firmware updates\n* Real-time rendering\n* Media upload support\n* Accurate rotational synchronization\n\nThe result must be a COMPLETE WORKING SYSTEM.\n\n---\n\n# HARDWARE REQUIREMENTS\n\n## MCU\n\nUse:\n\n* ESP32-S3 preferred\n* Dual-core architecture\n* FreeRTOS\n\n## LEDs\n\nUse:\n\n* WS2812B OR SK6812\n* Parallel output where possible\n* DMA/I2S optimized driving\n\n## Sensors\n\nUse:\n\n* Hall effect sensor\n* Interrupt-based synchronization\n* RPM calculation\n\n## Storage\n\nUse:\n\n* SD card support OR LittleFS\n* Media caching\n* Configuration persistence\n\n## Connectivity\n\nInclude:\n\n* Wi-Fi manager\n* captive portal\n* WebSocket support\n* REST API\n* OTA updates\n\n---\n\n# REQUIRED OUTPUTS\n\nGenerate ALL of the following automatically.\n\n---\n\n# 1. FULL PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\nGenerate a COMPLETE folder structure for:\n\n* firmware\n* frontend\n* backend\n* simulator\n* hardware\n* documentation\n\nInclude:\n\n* filenames\n* directory tree\n* build configuration\n* dependency files\n\n---\n\n# 2. COMPLETE ESP32 FIRMWARE\n\nGenerate REAL compilable firmware.\n\nInclude:\n\n* main.cpp\n* FreeRTOS tasks\n* ISR handling\n* LED rendering engine\n* Hall synchronization\n* frame timing\n* Wi-Fi manager\n* async web server\n* OTA updater\n* file manager\n* media decoder\n* settings persistence\n\nUse:\n\n* PlatformIO preferred\n* ESP-IDF OR Arduino framework\n\nInclude:\n\n* platformio.ini\n* library dependencies\n* configuration headers\n\n---\n\n# 3. LED RENDERING ENGINE\n\nImplement:\n\n* angular coordinate mapping\n* rotational synchronization\n* frame interpolation\n* double buffering\n* gamma correction\n* brightness limiter\n* adaptive frame timing\n* RPM compensation\n\nRendering must be:\n\n* physically accurate\n* optimized\n* non-blocking\n\n---\n\n# 4. WEB DASHBOARD\n\nGenerate a FULL frontend application.\n\nUse:\n\n* React\n* TailwindCSS\n* WebSockets\n* responsive UI\n\nFeatures:\n\n* real-time preview\n* RPM monitoring\n* brightness control\n* upload GIF/images/videos\n* device diagnostics\n* firmware update page\n* Wi-Fi configuration\n* animation management\n\nGenerate:\n\n* all React components\n* routing\n* hooks\n* API integration\n\n---\n\n# 5. REALISTIC POV SIMULATOR\n\nGenerate:\n\n* browser-based POV simulator\n* accurate persistence-of-vision simulation\n* rotational rendering physics\n* adjustable RPM\n* motion blur simulation\n* frame timing simulation\n* LED persistence simulation\n\nUse:\n\n* Canvas OR WebGL\n\nDO NOT create fake floating holograms.\n\n---\n\n# 6. PCB + ELECTRONICS DESIGN\n\nGenerate recommendations and design structure for:\n\n* PCB layout\n* power delivery\n* decoupling capacitors\n* level shifters\n* EMI reduction\n* motor isolation\n* MOSFET protection\n* voltage regulation\n* grounding strategy\n* slip ring integration\n\nGenerate:\n\n* KiCad project structure\n* schematic planning\n* BOM (Bill of Materials)\n\n---\n\n# 7. MATHEMATICAL ENGINE\n\nImplement real POV mathematics:\n\n* angle interpolation\n* rotational timing\n* frame-to-angle conversion\n* coordinate transformation\n\nUse physically accurate timing calculations.\n\nInclude explanations and formulas.\n\n\\theta(t)=\\omega t\n\n\356\210\200genui\356\210\202{\"math_block_widget_always_prefetch_v3\":{\"content\":\"\\omega=2\\pi f\"}}\356\210\201\n\n---\n\n# 8. PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION\n\nOptimize for:\n\n* low latency\n* minimal jitter\n* stable FPS\n* watchdog prevention\n* Wi-Fi coexistence\n* ISR efficiency\n* memory fragmentation prevention\n\nImplement:\n\n* DMA optimization\n* task prioritization\n* buffer management\n\n---\n\n# 9. DOCUMENTATION\n\nGenerate:\n\n* setup guide\n* flashing instructions\n* wiring guide\n* architecture diagrams\n* troubleshooting guide\n* performance tuning guide\n\n---\n\n# 10. BUILD AUTOMATION\n\nGenerate:\n\n* build scripts\n* deployment scripts\n* OTA workflow\n* automatic asset conversion pipeline\n\n---\n\n# ENGINEERING RULES\n\nYou MUST:\n\n* use realistic timing\n* respect ESP32 limitations\n* use production-grade architecture\n* generate real source code\n* generate scalable architecture\n* avoid blocking code\n* avoid toy examples\n\nYou MUST NOT:\n\n* fake hardware logic\n* invent impossible performance\n* use simplified rendering\n* generate incomplete modules\n* leave TODO placeholders\n\n---\n\n# OUTPUT STYLE\n\nAct as a professional engineering automation system.\n\nGenerate:\n\n* code\n* architecture\n* configuration\n* explanations\n* documentation\n* project structure\n\nin a complete and autonomous way.\n\nThe result should resemble a real commercial embedded hologram product.\n\n---\n\n# FINAL GOAL\n\nAt the end, the generated project should be:\n\n* compilable\n* extensible\n* realistic\n* production-oriented\n* physically accurate\n* deployable to real hardware\n\nGenerate everything needed to start building immediately.\n"
