  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining the System Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently taking stock of the codebase. It looks like we\'re starting with a React, Tailwind CSS, and Express web application template. The system design is for a production-grade rotating POV hologram, so I\'m focusing on how these components will support that goal. My next step will be mapping out the initial system architecture based on these technologies.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Requirements**\n\nI\'ve clarified the system\'s core function. It demands a sophisticated suite: a control dashboard, POV simulator, PCB guidance, BOM, KiCad organization, real-time math, and ESP32 firmware files, all integrated into a structured application. I am now prioritizing the interactive elements: a browser-based POV simulator with advanced rendering physics and a code generator panel for user-friendly access to the firmware.\n\n\n**Developing the Core Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core features. I\'m focusing on the configuration file updates to permit live code adjustment. Then, I am developing the hardware/PCB module, including BOMs, KiCad schematics and wiring helpers. The asset pipeline is a high priority, to handle image uploads, polar coordinate mapping and dynamic C++ header generation. Finally, I\'m setting up the control dashboard for device diagnostics and speed control.\n\n\n**Assessing AI Integration**\n\nI\'m now determining if incorporating Gemini API is beneficial. I\'ve considered its potential for asset generation or firmware customization. I can implement the needed functionality with either server-side or client-side Javascript. I\'m focusing on the modular design of a fully self-contained interactive application, with high visual polish and downloadable files. I will consider using `gemini-api`, but a self-contained Javascript version may be ideal.\n\n\n"
