    started_at {
      seconds: 1779364510
      nanos: 340146319
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering App Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on structuring the app, breaking it down into modular files for quality. The priority is the interactive POV simulator, specifically its canvas/WebGL implementation, adjustable RPM range, radius control, and LED strip configuration on each arm. I am paying close attention to the features requested, focusing on how these components integrate.\n\n\n**Refining POV Simulator**\n\nI\'m now integrating image uploading, polar coordinate downsampling, and real-time display into the interactive POV simulator. I\'m focusing on building beautiful React components that allow for custom image integration. I\'m exploring persistence factors for motion blur.\n\n\n**Calculating Technical Specs**\n\nI\'m now diving into the math and hardware aspects. I\'m focusing on a panel that will display the math behind the POV calculations, based on user-entered parameters like RPM and LED count. I\'m calculating frame angular resolution, microsecond-per-slice, linear speed, bandwidth requirements, and centrifugal force. I\'m also planning the hardware design features, including a BOM planner and PCB advice.\n\n\n**Analyzing Power Needs**\n\nI\'m now calculating power draw, like the peak amps at 5V for 270 LEDs plus the ESP32, and determining the recommended power supply/battery size. I\'m also considering an interactive KiCad PCB trace width calculator. I am now working on an interactive diagnostic dashboard to provide real-time monitoring and simulated telemetry data.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Features**\n\nI\'ve been working on interactive components for generating custom firmware, KiCad BOM advice, and a math engine. The firmware generator creates downloadable files from UI parameters, including an image data file. The hardware BOM component offers a calculator with pricing and power details, while the math engine displays equations and checks ESP32 capabilities. I am also working on an interactive dashboard to control the device and monitor its performance, plus a setup guide.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/types.ts` which declares the custom configurations, mathematical constraints, and shared data models for our ESP32 POV platform. This will maintain type safety throughout our simulator, firmware generator, and calculators."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 957301261
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
