    thinking: "**Integrating the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now diving into `App.tsx`! The goal is a truly next-level developer dashboard. I\'m focusing on seamless module integration. Before that, I\'m reviewing state setup, and I\'ve decided to track `firmwareConfig`. This is a critical first step.\n\n\n**Defining the Configs**\n\nI\'m structuring the core config states now. I\'ve defined `SSID`, `password`, `targetRpm`, and several pin definitions. I\'m also planning the `simulationConfig` to include parameters like `rpm`, `brightness`, and `sensorJitterUs`. Capturing live `diagnosticData` and `sampledPolarData` is key.\n\nI am also thinking about visual structure for `App.tsx` and taking into account the instructions provided to \"decide the mood (bold, minimal, warm, technical, playful)\" for the CSS design, defaulting to a clean, high-contrast light theme.\n\n\n**Refining the Aesthetic**\n\nI\'ve decided to embrace a dark mode aesthetic, leaning into a \"deep space blue\" tech terminal vibe. I\'m focusing on glowing slate, neon emerald accents, and a JetBrains Mono font. I\'m planning custom HUD grid overlays and micro-animations for a highly advanced feel. The layout will be responsive and organized with a major top header, main app layout, and several sub-sections that will organize data.\n\n\n**Structuring the Interface**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the layout. I\'m aiming for a two-column \"bento\" grid. The left side will feature the rotational POV physics simulator and captive portal controls. The right side will handle the embedded firmware compiler, hardware design with interactive BOM, and an assembly/operational engineering manual along with a mathematical physics solver. I\'m focusing on making sure all components and variables are linked and typed correctly.\n\n\n**Defining Core States**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the initial `firmwareConfig` and `simConfig` state definitions, along with the `diagnosticData` structure. These states are now defined with specific types and initial values, ready for integration into the dashboard\'s core functionality.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now edit `/src/App.tsx` to mount our interactive CAD and engineering simulator. This bundles the sub-stepped physics model, custom C++ downloader, real-time current calculators, board parameters, and math engines into a cohesive single-screen workspace."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 900021180
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
