    replacement_chunks {
      target_content: "export default function SetupGuide() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 text-slate-300 text-left\" id=\"assembly-documentation-manual\">\n      {/* Header */}\n      <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between pb-4 border-b border-slate-800 mb-6\">\n        <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n          <div className=\"p-2 bg-indigo-500/10 text-indigo-400 rounded-lg\">\n            <BookOpen className=\"w-5 h-5\" />\n          </div>\n          <div>\n            <h3 className=\"font-sans font-semibold text-slate-100 tracking-tight text-md\">Assembly & Operational Engineering Manual</h3>\n            <p className=\"font-mono text-slate-500 text-xs text-left\">Mechanical Dynamics, Flashing Protocols, & Balancing</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 leading-relaxed text-sm\">\n        \n        {/* Step 1: Mechanical Balancing */}\n        <div className=\"space-y-4 bg-slate-950 p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800\">\n          <h4 className=\"font-sans font-bold text-xs uppercase text-emerald-400 flex items-center gap-1.5 border-b border-slate-900 pb-2\">\n            <Compass className=\"w-4 h-4\" />\n            1. Rotor Mechanical Centroid Balancing\n          </h4>\n          <p className=\"text-xs text-slate-400 leading-normal\">\n            A dual-arm rotor spinning at 1200 RPM and 20cm length moves its tip at nearly <strong>90 km/h</strong>. Under <strong>1,610 G\'s of centrifugal pressure</strong>, any asymmetrical mass distributions creates deep lateral torque stress, leading to high-frequency structural vibration, sound pollution, motor bearing wear, and eventual joint rupture.\n          </p>\n          <ul className=\"text-xs space-y-2 text-slate-400 list-disc list-inside\">\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-slate-300\">Asymmetric Load balancing:</strong> If you place a heavier component (e.g., the ESP32 chip or buck converter) on Arm 1, you MUST secure a matching dummy counterweight (zinc solder clips or adhesive lead foils) at the exact radial distance on Arm 2.\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-slate-300\">Solder Joint Integrity:</strong> Under 1600+ Gs, the gravity mass pulls solder joints outward. Use standard cyanoacrylate structural glue or structural epoxy coatings on all component packages.\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-slate-300\">Aero Drag Reduction:</strong> Encapsulate the rotor blades within a clear circular acrylic dome to cut wind resistance, keep dust off LED beads, and prevent serious skin-injury points if touched.\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Step 2: Electrical Connection Schema */}\n        <div className=\"space-y-4 bg-slate-950 p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800\">\n          <h4 className=\"font-sans font-bold text-xs uppercase text-indigo-400 flex items-center gap-1.5 border-b border-slate-900 pb-2\">\n            <Settings className=\"w-4 h-4\" />\n            2. System Electrical Schematics\n          </h4>\n          <p className=\"text-xs text-slate-400 leading-normal\">\n            Proper signal topology is mandatory to keep logic and power rails clean. WS2812 communication requires rock-solid data frames that can fail under motor feedback:\n          </p>\n          <div className=\"font-mono text-[10px] bg-slate-900 leading-loose p-3 rounded text-indigo-300 border border-slate-850\">\n            {`  [STATIONARY Hub: Stator Base]\n  Power Source (12V/3A) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n                                    \342\224\202  (Capsule Slip Ring)\n  [SPINNING Plate: Rotor PCB]       \342\226\274\n  Core Slip-Ring (V+, GND) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 Buck Regulator (12V to 5V/5A Output)\n                                    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 WS2812 LED Power Rail (+5V, GND)\n                                    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 ESP32-S3 VCC & GND (+5V, GND)\n  \n  ESP32 Pin 12 (3.3V) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 Level Shifter (74HCT125) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 LED Line 1 (5V Data)\n  ESP32 Pin 13 (3.3V).\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 Level Shifter (74HCT125) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 LED Line 2 (5V Data)\n  Hall Sensor Pin 11  \342\227\204\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 Pulled High (10k Resistor to 3.3V)`}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Calibration section */}\n        <div className=\"space-y-4 bg-slate-950 p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800\">\n          <h4 className=\"font-sans font-bold text-xs uppercase text-amber-500 flex items-center gap-1.5 border-b border-slate-900 pb-2\">\n            <Sliders className=\"w-4 h-4\" />\n            3. Angular Synchronization Calibration\n          </h4>\n          <p className=\"text-xs text-slate-400 leading-normal\">\n            Physical magnet placement relative to the unipolar Hall sensor determines where the 0\302\260 absolute index coordinate lands on your rotor. If the magnet is offset, the rendering will appear skewed or upside-down.\n          </p>\n          <ul className=\"text-xs space-y-2 text-slate-400 list-disc list-inside\">\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-slate-300\">Magnetic Polarity:</strong> Unipolar sensors like AH3503 only trigger on a strong <strong>South pole face</strong>. If your index pin interrupt fails to fire, flip the stator magnet over.\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-slate-300\">Phase Offset Fine-Tuning:</strong> Rather than physically re-gluing the magnet, use the Web Panel\'s <strong>Calibrate Alignment Phase Offset slider</strong> or adjust the C++ variable <span className=\"font-mono bg-slate-900 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-amber-400\">sensor_phase_offset_rad</span> to compensate for the rotational skew!\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Technical Troubleshooting */}\n        <div className=\"space-y-4 bg-slate-950 p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800\">\n          <h4 className=\"font-sans font-bold text-xs uppercase text-rose-400 flex items-center gap-1.5 border-b border-slate-900 pb-2\">\n            <AlertTriangle className=\"w-4 h-4\" />\n            4. Critical Troubleshooting Matrix\n          </h4>\n          \n          <div className=\"space-y-2.5 text-xs\">\n            <div>\n              <strong className=\"text-slate-300 block\">Symptom: Dynamic Display Shear / Tearing</strong>\n              <span className=\"text-slate-400 text-[11px] block leading-normal\">\n                Reason: Sector timing calculations are colliding. Your rotor is spinning faster than your LED communication channel (WS2812\'s 800kHz speed limit). Reduce your slice divisions to 45 or integrate dedicated I2S DMA parallel strip driving to bypass communication delay.\n              </span>\n            </div>\n            <div>\n              <strong className=\"text-slate-300 block\">Symptom: High Jitter & Image Shaking</strong>\n              <span className=\"text-slate-400 text-[11px] block leading-normal\">\n                Reason: Motor ESC speed governing is fluctuating or interrupt is delayed. Isolate FastLED updates to Core 1 in firmware, and run Wi-Fi Webserver loops strictly on Core 0. Ensure no blocking <span className=\"font-mono bg-slate-950 px-1 text-rose-300\">delay()</span> statements exist in interrupt callbacks.\n              </span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n      </div>\n    </div>"
      replacement_content: "export default function SetupGuide() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"bg-[#0E1012] border border-[#2A2D33] rounded-sm p-6 text-slate-300 text-left\" id=\"assembly-documentation-manual\">\n      {/* Panel header */}\n      <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between pb-4 border-b border-[#2A2D33] mb-6\">\n        <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n          <div className=\"w-2.5 h-6 bg-[#00F0FF] rounded-none\"></div>\n          <div>\n            <h3 className=\"font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#E0E2E5] font-semibold\">06 // ASSEMBLY & OPERATIONAL ENGINEERING MANUAL</h3>\n            <p className=\"font-mono text-[#8E9299] text-[10px] uppercase\">Mechanical balancing dynamics // Interrupt sync protocols // Isolation</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 leading-relaxed text-sm\">\n        \n        {/* Step 1: Mechanical Balancing */}\n        <div className=\"space-y-4 bg-[#15171A] p-5 border border-[#2A2D33]\">\n          <h4 className=\"font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-[#00F0FF] tracking-wider border-l-2 border-[#00F0FF] pl-2 font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 pb-2 border-b border-[#2A2D33]\">\n            <Compass className=\"w-4 h-4 text-[#00F0FF]\" />\n            1. Rotor Mechanical Centroid Balancing\n          </h4>\n          <p className=\"text-[11px] text-[#8E9299] leading-relaxed font-mono uppercase\">\n            A dual-arm rotor spinning at 1200 RPM and 20cm length moves its tip at nearly <strong>90 km/h</strong>. Under <strong>1,610 G\'s of centrifugal pressure</strong>, any asymmetrical mass distributions creates deep lateral torque stress, leading to high-frequency structural vibration, sound pollution, motor bearing wear, and eventual joint rupture.\n          </p>\n          <ul className=\"text-[10px] space-y-2 text-[#8E9299] list-disc list-inside font-mono uppercase leading-relaxed\">\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-[#E0E2E5]\">Asymmetric load balancing:</strong> If you place a heavier component (e.g., the ESP32 chip or buck converter) on Arm 1, secure dummy weights (lead tape or metal rivets) on the opposite arm quadrant.\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-[#E0E2E5]\">Solder structural bond:</strong> Massive G-loading pulls components outward. Apply standard viscous cyanoacrylate adhesive or high-grade conformal coating on LED beads.\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-[#E0E2E5]\">Aero drag shielding:</strong> Enclose the spinning armature inside an acrylic safety dome to prevent high-speed particle collisions and protect hands.\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Step 2: Electrical Connection Schema */}\n        <div className=\"space-y-4 bg-[#15171A] p-5 border border-[#2A2D33]\">\n          <h4 className=\"font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-[#00F0FF] tracking-wider border-l-2 border-[#00F0FF] pl-2 font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 pb-2 border-b border-[#2A2D33]\">\n            <Settings className=\"w-4 h-4 text-[#00F0FF]\" />\n            2. System Electrical Schematics\n          </h4>\n          <p className=\"text-[10px] text-[#8E9299] leading-relaxed font-mono uppercase\">\n            Maintain rigorous separation of supply rails. Heavy brushless motor transient loads easily disrupt logic state machines:\n          </p>\n          <pre className=\"font-mono text-[9px] bg-[#000] p-3 rounded-none text-[#00F0FF] border border-[#2A2D33] overflow-x-auto leading-normal uppercase\">\n{`[STATIONARY Hub: Stator Base]\nPower Source (12V/3A) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n                                \342\224\202  (Capsule Slip Ring)\n[SPINNING Plate: Rotor PCB]       \342\226\274\nCore Slip-Ring (V+, GND) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 Buck Regulator (5V/5A Out)\n                                \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 LED Power Rail (5V, GND)\n                                \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 ESP32-S3 Pin VCC & GND\n  \nESP32 Pin 12 (3.3V) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 Level Shifter \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 LED Line 1 (5V Data)\nESP32 Pin 13 (3.3V) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 Level Shifter \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 LED Line 2 (5V Data)\nHall Sensor Pin 11  \342\227\204\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 Pullup Resistor to 3.3V`}\n          </pre>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Calibration section */}\n        <div className=\"space-y-4 bg-[#15171A] p-5 border border-[#2A2D33]\">\n          <h4 className=\"font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-[#FFB800] tracking-wider border-l-2 border-[#FFB800] pl-2 font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 pb-2 border-b border-[#2A2D33]\">\n            <Sliders className=\"w-4 h-4 text-[#FFB800]\" />\n            3. Angular Synchronization Calibration\n          </h4>\n          <p className=\"text-[11px] text-[#8E9299] leading-relaxed font-mono uppercase\">\n            The unipolar hall sensor provides the physical 0\302\260 trigger datum. Any angular misalignment causes projected hologram geometries to appear visually rotated or upside-down.\n          </p>\n          <ul className=\"text-[10px] space-y-2 text-[#8E9299] list-disc list-inside font-mono uppercase leading-relaxed\">\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-[#E0E2E5]\">Magnetic Polarity:</strong> Unipolar latches like AH3503 only trigger on a strong <strong>South pole face</strong>. If state triggers fail to interrupt, invert the stator magnet direction.\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <strong className=\"text-[#E0E2E5]\">Digital Skew Tuning:</strong> Rather than physical adjustments, use the dynamic **Phase Offset Calibration** slider or configure the C++ variable <span className=\"font-mono bg-[#000] px-1 py-0.5 border border-[#2A2D33] text-[#FFB800]\">sensor_phase_offset_rad</span> in software.\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Technical Troubleshooting */}\n        <div className=\"space-y-4 bg-[#15171A] p-5 border border-[#2A2D33]\">\n          <h4 className=\"font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-[#FF4E00] tracking-wider border-l-2 border-[#FF4E00] pl-2 font-bold flex items-center gap-1.5 pb-2 border-b border-[#2A2D33]\">\n            <AlertTriangle className=\"w-4 h-4 text-[#FF4E00]\" />\n            4. Critical Troubleshooting Matrix\n          </h4>\n          \n          <div className=\"space-y-4 text-[10px] font-mono uppercase leading-relaxed\">\n            <div className=\"border-b border-[#2A2D33]/40 pb-2\">\n              <strong className=\"text-[#E0E2E5] block font-mono\">Symptom: Display Shear & Angular Tearing</strong>\n              <span className=\"text-[#8E9299] text-[9.5px] block leading-relaxed mt-1\">\n                Reason: Sector frame updates overlapping. Core pixel communications (WS2812 speed cap 800kHz) is bottlenecking. Reduce target sector subdivisions or split strips across parallel I2S hardware registers.\n              </span>\n            </div>\n            <div>\n              <strong className=\"text-[#E0E2E5] block font-mono\">Symptom: High Spatial Jitter</strong>\n              <span className=\"text-[#8E9299] text-[9.5px] block leading-relaxed mt-1\">\n                Reason: Fluctuations in rotor angular rate. Isolate FastLED updates to Core 1 in firmware, and run Wi-Fi server loops strictly on Core 0. Eliminate block-level delay commands across routines.\n              </span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}"
    }
