  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Summarizing Our Accomplishments**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve just seen the build succeed! The applet compiled without a hitch. My next step is to neatly summarize everything, using clear and concise language. I\'ll make sure to state all the actions right away and give descriptions.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Details**\n\nI\'m now focused on distilling the implementation into elegant, scannable bullet points. My goal is to clearly detail the visual choices, physical formulas, and interactivity, without resorting to code-level jargon or unnecessary features. I\'m prioritizing a professional tone and maintaining composure. I will cease any further actions to stay within the original requests.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully enhanced the rotating POV hologram platform with production-grade firmware error handling, a refined visual rendering engine, and dynamic telemetry graphs.\n\n### Summary of Enhancements\n\n1. **Hardware-Aware Firmware Error Handling**:\n   - **Non-Blocking Wi-Fi Reconnection**: Introduced background Wi-Fi event handler loops in the generated C++ `main.cpp` code. This allows the system to auto-reconnect or fall back to an internal Access Point without locking up high-speed rendering threads.\n   - **Rotor Stall & Thermal Spot Protection**: Implemented an index interrupt watchdog inside the core thread. If the sensor misses a trigger for more than `500 ms`, FastLED shuts down its power channels to protect stationary led strips from localized heat damage.\n   - **Current Overload & Voltage Sag Mitigation**: Configured FastLED\342\200\231s high-precision power regulator to throttle brightness dynamically below a standard `3000 mA` limit, preventing browser-side brownouts or slip-ring damage.\n\n2. **Refined Physics-First simulator**:\n   - **Continuous Vector Arc Sweeps**: Upgraded the canvas rendering engine to draw continuous vector arcs representing the exact sweeping motion of each LED during the slice sub-step. This creates smooth, motion-blurred visuals at higher RPMs instead of dotted segmentation.\n   - **Frame-Rate Independent Retinal Decay**: Replaced simple frame overlays with an exponential decay mathematical model based on biological visual persistence (in milliseconds). This guarantees identical visual fading rates regardless of browser frame-rate performance.\n   - **Dedicated Time Constant Sliders**: Added bi-directionally synchronized sliders in the physics panel, giving users direct control over physiological visual retention (from rapid discharge to slow combustion).\n\n3. **High-Tech Real-Time Telemetry & Fault Injection Console**:\n   - **Active Waveform Plot Analyzer**: Created a dual-mode telemetry board. Users can toggle between digital columns and glowing real-time SVG wave plots tracing **RPM Speed**, **FreeRTOS CPU Scheduler Load**, and **Stator Thermal Planes**.\n   - **Blinking Tracer Pulsars**: The vector plots render custom grid lines, glowing linear gradients, and a blinking pulse point tracking the live streaming telemetry header.\n   - **Direct Fault Injectors**: Added interactive fault triggers (**Wi-Fi Dropout**, **Sensor Stall**, and **Voltage Sag**) allowing you to simulate critical conditions, watch the diagnostic lines change state, and read the C++ recovery sequences inside the WebSocket stream."
