    thinking: "**Analyzing LED Communication Errors**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the ESP32 firmware\'s LED rendering engine. My latest task is to incorporate checks for FastLED communication errors. I intend to log these specific LED strip issues via WebSocket to the dashboard. The goal is to pinpoint exactly which strip is experiencing glitches or data line problems.\n\n\n**Refining LED Error Detection**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into error detection methods. I\'ve uncovered existing checks for data line glitches within the dashboard\'s connection logic, specifically looking at impedance mismatch or shorted lines. Now, I\'m focusing on augmenting this with FastLED\'s built-in error checks and software-based CRCs for more robust monitoring of LED strip issues.\n\n\n**Investigating FastLED Error Checking**\n\nI\'m revisiting the FastLED library to see how it handles communication errors. Specifically, I\'m checking for APIs like `FastLED.getWriteError()`. I\'m comparing this to the existing `verifyLineIntegrity()` function, which seems to perform hardware pin-level checks. The goal is to figure out whether the library can provide a higher level check or if we are the high-level check, to incorporate robust dynamic error detection for our LED strips.\n\n\n"
